WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.321
"Mercury in High Fructose Corn Syrup"

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.080
Whether you feed people honey,
table sugar,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.800
or high-fructose corn syrup,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.000
you see similarly negative
metabolic effects.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.840
A meta-analysis
of all such studies

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.880
found there didn't appear
to be any difference

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.120
between the negative effects
of high-fructose corn syrup

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.200
and table sugar on body fat,
blood pressure, blood sugars,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.880
triglycerides, or cholesterol.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.120
But high-fructose corn syrup
did appear to be

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.600
more pro-inflammatory.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.000
One thing that sets apart
corn syrup from sugar

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.320
is mercury,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.920
detected in about half
the samples

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.680
of high-fructose corn syrup
analyzed.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.640
In terms of diet, mercury is
routinely detected in fish,

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.640
but it's also found
in other meat like poultry

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.600
because farmers routinely feed
fishmeal to chickens,

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.560
but how is mercury
getting into corn syrup?

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.080
Everything you wanted to know
but were afraid to ask.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.200
It turns out mercury can enter
the corn sweetener market line

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.000
in one of two ways:

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.080
the use
of mercury-processed chemicals

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.640
in the manufacturing process

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.200
or the intentional addition

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.720
of mercury-containing chemicals.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.400
Either way, does it actually
make it to the consumer?

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.400
Researchers looked
at 50 different brands of foods

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.000
containing corn syrup,
from soda pop to Pop-Tarts,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.840
Yoplait yogurt, jelly.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.040
The results?

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.440
About 30 percent
were contaminated

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.800
with detectable levels
of mercury.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.520
Enough to be harmful?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.600
With the average
daily consumption of corn syrup,

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.200
and how much mercury
they found,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.360
the potential average
daily total mercury exposure

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.760
from high-fructose corn syrup

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.720
could range from zero
to 28 micrograms.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.640
This range can be compared
to the range

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.000
of total mercury exposure

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.400
from those silvery dental
amalgam mercury fillings

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.520
we get for cavities.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.240
Canada and other countries
recommend

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.280
against the use
of mercury amalgam

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.760
in pregnant women or children,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.280
as does the United States
as of 2020.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.680
Of course, a single can of tuna

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.320
can have as much mercury
as a whole cup (240 ml)

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.160
of high-fructose corn syrup.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:02.080
But still,
we probably shouldn't let

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.960
our kids become
children of the corn.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.360
Given its mercury
contamination,

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.080
one could argue
that high-fructose corn syrup

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.440
is worse than sugar.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.200
But both are bad for us.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.720
They're both
just empty calories,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.040
calories with zero nutrition.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.080
Check out this classic
sugar industry ad:

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.600
"If sugar is so fattening,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.680
how come so many kids
are thin?"

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.760
That certainly can't
be said anymore.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.920
The tagline?

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.880
"Sugar.
It's not just good flavor;

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.840
sugar is good food."

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.040
As unbelievable
as that one was,

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.000
this is my favorite:

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.720
Mary is a busy girl.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.280
"She needs sugar in her life.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.160
For energy.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.360
She needs energyless,
artificial sweeteners

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.920
like a turtle
needs a seat belt."

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.080
"...18 calories per teaspoon
and it's all energy."

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.520
That's the problem!

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.480
Only the sugar industry could
take its greatest weakness--

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.120
empty calories--

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.120
and try to spin it
into something good.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.200
"Note to Mothers: Play it safe
with your young ones—

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.080
make sure they get sugar
every day."

